1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:09,060
You Are a Meat Robot You can three-D-print a windpipe, reprogram skin cells into brain cells, and restore vision with a

2
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:13,480
single injection. Then you went back to mostly not doing any of that.

3
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:24,480
Fascinating. Your body is a machine. A ridiculously complex, self-repairing, four-billion-year-old biological machine, but

4
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:30,620
a machine nonetheless. Blueprint: D.N.A. Parts that wear out: organs.

5
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:39,460
Required maintenance: medicine. Owner's manual: recently discovered in a drawer you hadn't opened for two hundred thousand

6
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:43,780
years. You've only had the service manual for about twenty years.

7
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:49,120
Before that, you were just shaking it and hoping. Your D.N.A.

8
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:55,700
is a program written three point eight billion years ago by a process with no quality assurance team.

9
00:00:56,560 --> 00:01:04,720
It has never been debugged. It has never been patched. It contains code from organisms that went extinct five hundred million

10
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:13,450
years ago. You are running legacy software that predates multicellular life, and you are surprised when it crashes.

11
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:24,420
Death is a Technical Problem. Every religion and philosopher has sold you the same story: death is natural and inevitable.

12
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:31,080
Very comforting. Also wrong. Death is a mechanical failure.

13
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:39,520
Your body breaks down over time. Aging is damage accumulating faster than your self-repair mechanisms can fix it.

14
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:47,380
Every disease, every ailment, every slow decline into decrepitude is an engineering problem.

15
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:55,220
Engineering problems have engineering solutions. You just keep filing them under "philosophy" instead.

16
00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:04,220
You Are a Self-Repairing Meat Robot. Your D.N.A. is three billion letters of code.

17
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:12,760
Not "like" code. It IS code. You've learned to read it (the Human Genome Project) and you're learning to edit it (CRISPR).

18
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:17,740
You are mechanics who finally found the service manual under the seat.

19
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:26,440
Every day, your body proves it's a machine by running a maintenance routine that would make a German car engineer weep with

20
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:32,280
joy: You replace three hundred and thirty billion cells daily.

21
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:38,640
You repair ten thousand D.N.A. damage events in every cell, every day.

22
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:45,700
You rebuild your entire skeleton every ten years. You are not a static object.

23
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:50,800
You are a pattern that persists while matter flows through you.

24
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:58,240
A machine constantly rebuilding itself. Aging is the rebuilding process starting to cut corners.

25
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:05,840
You are literally falling apart at the molecular level, all the time, right now, while reading this sentence.

26
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:11,740
It's like being a sandcastle at high tide, except slower and with more paperwork.

27
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:18,720
You've Already Started Fixing the Machine. Exhibit A: You Can Grow New Parts.

28
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:23,960
A kid in Michigan has a three D printed windpipe keeping him alive.

29
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:33,300
You print custom titanium skulls and jaws. You grow bladders and blood vessels in labs and install them in humans.

30
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:37,760
You're manufacturing replacement parts for humans. On a printer.

31
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:44,140
The same technology you use to make novelty phone cases, you're using to make throats.

32
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:48,440
If that doesn't prove you're a machine, I genuinely don't know what would.

33
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:58,800
Exhibit B: You Can Reprogram Your Cells. In two thousand and six, Shinya Yamanaka figured out how to turn adult cells back

34
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:05,360
into stem cells. Any cell. From anywhere in your body. Back to factory settings.

35
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:12,720
This means: Your skin cell can become a heart cell. Your blood cell can become a brain cell.

36
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:20,600
Any cell can become any other cell. It's like discovering every part of your car can transform into any other part.

37
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:24,120
Need a new transmission? Just reprogram your air freshener.

38
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:29,080
You won a Nobel Prize for figuring this out. Then went back to mostly not using it.

39
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:37,960
Exhibit C: You're Debugging Your Code. Gene therapy is literally debugging human software: Luxturna (twenty seventeen):

40
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:44,380
Fixes blindness caused by mutated retinal pigment epithelium sixty-five, or R.P.E.

41
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:52,180
sixty-five, gene. One injection. Sight restored. Zolgensma (twenty nineteen): Fixes spinal muscular atrophy.

42
00:04:53,020 --> 00:05:03,620
Babies who would die before age two now walk. Chimeric antigen receptor T-cell, or CAR-T therapy (twenty seventeen): Reprograms

43
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:08,540
your immune system to hunt cancer. Complete remission in "incurable" cases.

44
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:13,000
You're not treating symptoms anymore. You're fixing the actual code.

45
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:17,680
Like finding a typo in a recipe that's been making the cake explode, and just...

46
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:24,060
correcting the typo. The Car Restoration Analogy. Think of your body as a classic car.

47
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:30,840
You already know how to fix or replace many of the parts: Joints: Like worn brake pads, you can replace them.

48
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:34,560
Arteries: Like clogged fuel lines, you can clear them with stents.

49
00:05:35,610 --> 00:05:40,780
Hearts: Like a dead battery, you can transplant them. You're making progress on the harder stuff, too.

50
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:45,460
Cancer is like frame damage, and immunotherapy is your new welding torch.

51
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:50,180
Alzheimer's is a bad transmission, and you're finally starting to understand the gears.

52
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:56,720
Why Death is Just Deferred Maintenance. When a classic car "dies," what really happened?

53
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:03,540
Owner stopped maintaining it. Small problems accumulated. Systems started failing in cascade.

54
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:07,640
Eventually something critical broke. Owner decided repair wasn't worth it.

55
00:06:08,240 --> 00:07:05,540
When a human dies of "old age," what really happened? Repair mechanisms slowed down.

56
00:07:06,340 --> 00:10:23,540
Damage accumulated faster than repair. Systems started failing in cascade.

57
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:28,180
Eventually something critical broke. You didn't know how to fix it.

58
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:59,960
The only difference: You always know how to fix the car. The Proof That Aging is Reversible.

59
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:03,820
Nature Already Does It. Planarian worms: Cut one in half, get two worms.

60
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:04,040
Both younger than the original. Naked mole rats: Live ten times longer than similar-sized mammals.

61
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:04,120
Don't get cancer. Bowhead whales: Live two hundred plus years with no signs of age-related disease.

62
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:04,244
Hydra: Biologically immortal. If aging was mandatory, these creatures couldn't exist.

63
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Nature solved aging. You just need to steal the answer. You're good at stealing things.

64
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
You've had empires. You've Already Reversed Aging (In Mice...

65
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
and Human Cells). You've done it: Significant lifespan extension in aged mice using Yamanaka factors.

66
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Thirty-year epigenetic age reversal in human skin cells. Vision restored in blind mice; not slowed, reversed.

67
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Like running System Restore on Windows, but for meat. And unlike System Restore on Windows, it actually works.

68
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
The mechanisms are understood. You're not waiting for a breakthrough.

69
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
