70
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Scientists originally identified nine hallmarks of aging, later expanded to twelve.

71
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Every one is a mechanical problem with a mechanical solution: Number one: genomic instability is addressed by gene editing,

72
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
like CRISPR. Number two: telomere shortening is addressed by telomerase activation.

73
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Number three: epigenetic alterations are addressed by cellular reprogramming.

74
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Number four: protein dysfunction is addressed by autophagy enhancement.

75
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Number five: nutrient sensing is addressed by metabolic manipulation.

76
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Number six: mitochondrial dysfunction is addressed by mitochondrial replacement.

77
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Number seven: cellular senescence is addressed by senolytic drugs.

78
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Number eight: stem cell exhaustion is addressed by stem cell therapy.

79
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Number nine: altered communication is addressed by system recalibration.

80
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
And the three newer hallmarks you discovered since: Number ten: disabled macroautophagy is addressed by autophagy inducers,

81
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
such as rapamycin analogs and spermidine. Number eleven: chronic inflammation is addressed by targeted anti-inflammatory

82
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
therapies (senolytics again, plus interleukin-six, or I.L. six, inhibitors).

83
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Number twelve: dysbiosis is addressed by microbiome restoration, such as fecal transplants and precision probiotics.

84
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Twelve problems. Twelve proposed solution pathways. You're not waiting for magic.

85
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
You're working through a checklist. You love checklists. Why You Haven't Been Fixed Yet (It's Just Money).

86
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
The Manhattan Project for Not Dying. The Manhattan Project cost roughly thirty billion dollars (adjusted for inflation)

87
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
and took three years. Result: nuclear weapons. You moved fast when the goal was killing two hundred thousand people in an

88
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
afternoon. You spend sixty-seven point five billion dollars per year globally on all medical research combined.

89
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
For everything. Cancer, Alzheimer's, heart disease, aging, rare diseases.

90
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Everything. That's your entire "not dying" budget. The Economics of Mortality.

91
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Here's why you're still dying: Pharmaceutical companies make money treating disease, not curing it (a cured patient is a

92
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
