93
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Military contractors have better lobbyists than dying people (dying people are busy dying).

94
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Your car mechanic has better diagnostic tools than your doctor.

95
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
A one percent treaty fixes this by making cures more profitable than treatments.

96
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
The Conclusion. Your body is not a mystical entity. It is a machine.

97
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
Every disease is a broken part. Every death is a mechanical failure you didn't fix in time.

98
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
This is not a metaphor. This is literally what is happening to you right now.

99
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
You can read the blueprint (D.N.A.), edit the code (CRISPR), and replace the parts (organ transplants).

100
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
The bottleneck isn't knowledge. It's priority. You have millions of untested repairs sitting on the shelf gathering dust

101
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
while you fund new ways to make other machines stop working.

102
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
The question isn't whether you CAN fix the human body. The question is whether you'll fund the mechanics before the warranty

103
00:11:04,244 --> 00:11:04,244
